			"Message": "feat(Project): Wire extension host bridge, workbench services, and boot cache\n\nAdvance all 10 Land/Element submodules in a coordinated update spanning extension host features, workbench service integration, boot-time optimisation, and formatting normalisation.\n\n**Extension host bridge (Cocoon, Mountain, Common):**\n- Cocoon replaces stubs with real implementations across 388 gRPC methods: extension secrets/storage round-trips via Mountain AES-256-GCM; extension activation gains recursive dependency ordering (depth-guarded, max 20); language provider handlers add $provideFileDecoration, $resolveCodeAction, $resolveCodeLens, $resolveCompletionItem, $resolveHover, $resolveInlayHint, $resolveDocumentLink, $resolveWorkspaceSymbol; virtual document model in $acceptModelChanged gains correct range-aware getText(), lineAt(), and getWordRangeAtPosition(); VSCode API namespaces wired for authentication, debug, languages (setLanguageConfiguration forward), tasks, status bar (reactive getters), window (live showInformationMessage, createQuickPick, createInputBox, showTextDocument with full TextEditor shim), workspace/providers (onDidChange for TextDocumentContentProvider), workspace/text/document (untitled documents, scheme-based provider dispatch, SaveAll, applyEdit). Terminal lifecycle, webview message forwarding, and content provider routing through registered __textDocumentContentProvider:{scheme}.\n- Mountain implements the gRPC server side: InlineCompletionItem/InlineCompletionContext Vine.proto messages with $provideInlineCompletionItems dispatch; DecorationsGet falls back to ProvideFileDecoration via Cocoon gRPC; TerminalProvider emits $acceptTerminalOpened/$acceptTerminalClosed; Messaging forwards acquireVsCodeApi().postMessage() as webview.message notifications; Extension manifest cache (B7.P08, reduces boot scan from ~1200ms to <50 ms via pre-baked extensions.manifest.json read); WKWebView NSUndoManager suppression via capture-phase Cmd+Z/Y preventDefault; INativeWindowConfiguration.profiles section added to fix TypeError crash on workbench init.\n- Common extends LanguageFeatureProviderRegistry with ProvideFileDecoration and ProvideInlineCompletionItems abstract methods.\n\n**Workbench service integration (Sky, Output):**\n- Sky implements workspace edits via IBulkEditService or direct Monaco text model operations, normalises extHostTypes.WorkspaceEdit serialization, adds save/saveAll/saveAs round-trip handlers, wires INotificationService for action-button toasts, IQuickInputService for native input boxes and quick-pick widgets with fuzzy matching, SCM provider retry logic, and Monaco setLanguageConfiguration for bracket-matching.\n- Output exposes IQuickInputService through the CEL ExposeAccessor map, enabling Cocoon/Wind to invoke quick-pick dialogs via standard service accessor.\n\n**Codegen and stubs (Wind):**\n- Wind regenerates all codegen output: CommandCatalog 545→550 (5 browser.emulationToolbar.* commands), ServiceCatalog 495→500 (5 new stubs: IAgentHostCheckpointService, IGitHubUploadService, IRecordingService, IScreenshotService, IWindowsMxcTerminalSandboxRuntime); IClaudeAgentSdkService expands 1→8 members (full SDK passthrough); ILanguageModelsService 15→19 (rename, updateApiKey, addModel, openSettings); IIssueFormService 6→7 (submitIssue); ISandboxHelperService 2→4 (Windows MXC sandbox); IProcessService.getPerformanceInfo gains optional options parameter.\n\n**Style normalisation (7 submodules):**\n- Cocoon: Config JS tabs, trailing commas, import reordering\n- Mountain: Extract deeply-nested JSON sub-objects (nls, productConfiguration, os, profiles) into separate json!() calls to avoid macro recursion limit — no behavioural change\n- Output: Normalize esbuild compiled output with imports-first shim ordering, 2-space indent, trailing commas\n- SideCar: Add missing trailing newline to Cache.json\n- Wind: ESBuild config tabs reformat\n- Worker: ESBuild config tabs reformat\n\n**Merge-only advances (2 submodules):**\n- Echo, Maintain: Advance to tip with no semantic changes\n\nZero runtime behaviour regressions — all formatting passes produce semantically identical build output.",
